This project is built for the openvela/NuttX ecosystem and uses openvela
components, board support code, audio drivers, graphics drivers, and build
integration when linked into an openvela workspace. Those upstream components
retain their original licenses and notices in the openvela source tree.

The audio-event application uses third-party open-source software through the
openvela apps tree, including TensorFlow Lite Micro, FlatBuffers, KissFFT, LVGL,
gemmlowp, and ruy. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the dependency and license
summary.

The current model and evaluation artifacts were produced from a mixed audio
dataset containing selected samples derived from FSD50K, ESC-50, and
self-collected recordings. The source datasets retain their own licenses and
attribution requirements. FSD50K contains clips with mixed Creative Commons
licenses. ESC-50 is distributed as a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial
dataset. Self-collected recordings are project data unless otherwise stated.
See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and docs/项目基线/性能与评估.md.
